%N A399072 Least positive number which can be expressed as the sum of some of its anti-divisors in exactly n ways.
%C A399072 All terms are pseudo anti-perfect numbers (A192270).
%H A399072 Paolo P. Lava, <a href="/A399072/b399072.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%e A399072 a(0) = 1 -> no anti-divisors.
%e A399072 a(1) = 5 -> anti-divisors of 5 are 2, 3 and: 2 + 3 = 5;
%e A399072 a(2) = 38 -> anti-divisors of 38 are 3, 4, 5, 7, 11, 15, 25 and: 3 + 4 + 5 + 11 + 15 = 5 + 7 + 11 + 15 = 38; etc.
